  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given:\n\n\ntwo arrays AAA and BBB, each consisting of NNN positive integers;\na positive integer KKK.\nFor a positive integer XXX, we say a set of indices {i1,i2,i3,…,im}\\{i_1, i_2, i_3, \\ldots, i_m\\}{i1​,i2​,i3​,…,im​} (where 1≤ij,m≤N1 \\leq i_j, m \\leq N1≤ij​,m≤N) to be X-good if:\n\n(Ai1(A_{i_1}(Ai1​​ ∣|∣ Ai2A_{i_2}Ai2​​ ∣|∣ Ai3A_{i_3}Ai3​​ ∣|∣ …\\ldots… ∣|∣ Aim)≤XA_{i_m}) \\leq XAim​​)≤X, where ∣|∣ denotes the bitwise or operation.\n\nThe goodness of an X-good set of indices {i1,i2,i3,…,im}\\{i_1, i_2, i_3, \\ldots, i_m\\}{i1​,i2​,i3​,…,im​} is defined as the sum of the corresponding elements from array BBB, i.e., Bi1+Bi2+Bi3+…+BimB_{i_1} + B_{i_2} + B_{i_3} + \\ldots + B_{i_m}Bi1​​+Bi2​​+Bi3​​+…+Bim​​.\n\nFor each integer 1≤X≤K1 \\leq X \\leq K1≤X≤K, find out the total goodness over all possible X-good set of indices. Since this number can be huge, print it modulo 109+710^9+7109+7.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and KKK — the number of elements in array AAA, and the parameter KKK.\nThe second line of each test case contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,A3,…,ANA_1, A_2, A_3,\\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,A3​,…,AN​, the elements of array AAA.\nThe third line of each test case contains NNN space-separated integers B1,B2,B3,…,BNB_1, B_2, B_3,\\ldots,B_NB1​,B2​,B3​,…,BN​, the elements of array BBB.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output KKK space-separated integers on a new line, where the ithi^{th}ith integer (1≤i≤K)(1 \\leq i \\leq K)(1≤i≤K) denotes the total goodness over all possible i-good set of indices modulo 109+710^9+7109+7.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤2⋅1051 \\leq N \\leq 2\\cdot 10^51≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤K≤1061 \\leq K \\leq 10^61≤K≤106",
      "1≤Ai≤K1 \\leq A_i \\leq K1≤Ai​≤K",
      "1≤Bi≤1091 \\leq B_i \\leq 10^91≤Bi​≤109",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 2⋅1052\\cdot 10^52⋅105.",
      "The sum of KKK over all test cases won't exceed 10610^6106."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n3 3\n1 2 3\n1 2 2\n2 2\n1 1\n1 2",
        "output": "1 3 20\n6 6",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: For each 1≤X≤K1 \\leq X \\leq K1≤X≤K:\n\nFor X=1:X=1:X=1: only good set of indices is {1}\\{1\\}{1}, hence the total goodness is B1=1B_1 = 1B1​=1.\nFor X=2:X=2:X=2: good set of indices are {1}\\{1\\}{1} and {2}\\{2\\}{2}, with goodness B1=1B_1=1B1​=1 and B2=2B_2=2B2​=2 respectively. Hence the total goodness is 333.\nFor X=3:X=3:X=3: good set of indices are {1}\\{1\\}{1} as (A1≤3)(A_1 \\leq 3)(A1​≤3), {2}\\{2\\}{2} as (A2≤3)(A_2 \\leq 3)(A2​≤3), {3}\\{3\\}{3} as (A1≤3)(A_1 \\leq 3)(A1​≤3), {1,2}\\{1, 2\\}{1,2} as (A1(A_1(A1​ ∣|∣ A2A_2A2​ ≤3)\\leq 3)≤3), {1,3}\\{1, 3\\}{1,3} as (A1(A_1(A1​ ∣|∣ A3A_3A3​ ≤3)\\leq 3)≤3), {2,3}\\{2, 3\\}{2,3} as (A2(A_2(A2​ ∣|∣ A3A_3A3​ ≤3)\\leq 3)≤3), {1,2,3}\\{1, 2, 3\\}{1,2,3} as (A1(A_1(A1​ ∣|∣ A2A_2A2​ ∣|∣ A3A_3A3​ ≤3)\\leq 3)≤3). Hence the total goodness is 1+2+2+(1+2)+(1+2)+(2+2)+(1+2+2)=201+2+2+(1+2)+(1+2)+(2+2)+(1+2+2)=201+2+2+(1+2)+(1+2)+(2+2)+(1+2+2)=20.\n\nTest case 222: For each 1≤X≤K1 \\leq X \\leq K1≤X≤K:\n\nFor X=1:X=1:X=1: good set of indices are {1}\\{1\\}{1}, {2}\\{2\\}{2}, {1,2}\\{1, 2\\}{1,2}. Hence the total goodness is 1+2+(1+2)=61+2+(1+2)=61+2+(1+2)=6.\nFor X=2:X=2:X=2: good set of indices are {1}\\{1\\}{1}, {2}\\{2\\}{2}, {1,2}\\{1, 2\\}{1,2}. Hence the total goodness is 1+2+(1+2)=61+2+(1+2)=61+2+(1+2)=6."
      }
    ]
  },
